### The Theory of the 4 Directions
Think of Otto's feet like the two treads on a tank:

Forward: Left foot twists negative, Right foot twists positive.

Backward: We reverse the pivots. Left foot twists positive, Right foot twists negative.

Turn Left: Both feet twist in the same negative direction. (This is exactly the "turning in circles" bug you accidentally discovered earlier—now we are using it on purpose!)

Turn Right: Both feet twist in the same positive direction.

